The code uses mutexes from the pthread library to ensure that concurrent access to the hash table is thread-safe. This prevents race conditions and ensures that only one thread can modify the hash table at a time.

Note that this code does not include error handling for memory allocation failures, which you should add in a real-world scenario. Additionally, it does not include logging or performance optimization features as requested in the task description. These would be important to consider for a production-quality implementation.']

